{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement","id":1230422,"title":"Rough idea for a werewolf mini-supplement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-26T17:56:59-07:00","id":1230422,"title":"Rough idea for a werewolf mini-supplement","content":"While eating, I was idly thinking and came up with an idea which could be easily tied to my earlier <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\">Bunyip</a> idea.<br /> <br /> In short, the pack locate and trace a Wyrm creature to South or Southeast Asia. Biting more than they can chew, they hear a strange whistling, which is oddly familiar, before a pack of unknown Fera comes our of the Umbra and help them defeat the creature.<br /> <br /> The Fera then celebrate the victorious Battle is a very familiar way that makes them ill at ease, but before they can do or say anything, they here a voice speaking in the Garou tongue behind them. The voice belong to an old Stargazer and his Beast Court pack. The old Stargazer, a Half-moon is torn. The pack prouved resourceful, in locating and in their valiant attempt to destroy the Wyrm taint, but in doing so have stumbled upon a Secret of the Emerald Court that they had keep for countless Centuries and would prefer to keep out of Garou Nation's collective Radar.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the unkown Fera are a group of Dhole shifter. Either a whole &quot;new&quot; race of Fera, with it's own role &amp; Auspices (something in the range of the Gaillard but without the storyteller/living memory element) or a offshoot/sub-tribe of the pre-Thylacine Bunyip...in which case they would be essentially Garou with a twist...ranging in 